{"name":"Delusional Dragonfly","hex":"#66bbcc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"delusional","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Suffering from delusions; having false or faulty beliefs.","Being, in the form of, or relating to, a delusion."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person suffering from a delusion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delusional"},{"term":"dragonfly","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An insect of the suborder Epiprocta or, more strictly, the infraorder Anisoptera, having four long transparent wings held perpendicular to a long body when perched."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dragonfly"}],"entries":[{"title":"Delusion","blocks":[{"text":"A delusion is a fixed belief that is not amenable to change in light of conflicting evidence. As a pathology, it is distinct from a belief based on false or incomplete information, confabulation, dogma, illusion, hallucination, or some other misleading effects of perception, as individuals with those beliefs are able to change or readjust their beliefs upon reviewing the evidence. However:"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delusion","wikidata":"Q189643"},{"title":"Dragonfly","blocks":[{"text":"A dragonfly is a flying insect belonging to the suborder Anisoptera of the order Odonata. About 3,000 living species of dragonflies are known. Most are tropical, with fewer species in temperate regions. Loss of wetland habitat threatens dragonfly populations around the world. Adult dragonflies are characterised by a pair of large, multifaceted, compound eyes, two pairs of strong, transparent wings, sometimes with coloured patches, and an elongated body. Many dragonflies have brilliant iridescent or metallic colours produced by structural coloration, making them conspicuous in flight. An adult dragonfly's compound eyes have nearly 24,000 ommatidia each."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Red_grasshawk_%28Neurothemis_fluctuans%29_male_Phuket_2.jpg/330px-Red_grasshawk_%28Neurothemis_fluctuans%29_male_Phuket_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragonfly","wikidata":"Q80066"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Airloom.gif/500px-Airloom.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Airloom.gif/500px-Airloom.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"James Tilly Matthews illustrated this picture of a machine called an \"air loom\", which he believed was being used to torture him and others for political purposes.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAirloom.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Meganeura.png/500px-Meganeura.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Meganeura.png/1280px-Meganeura.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Meganeura.png/500px-Meganeura.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The giant Upper Carboniferous dragonfly relative, Meganeura monyi, attained a wingspan around 680 millimetres (27 inches).[8]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMeganeura.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Mesurupetala%2C_dragonfly%2C_Late_Late_Jurassic%2C_Tithonian_Age%2C_Solnhofen_Lithographic_Limestone%2C_Solnhofen%2C_Bavaria%2C_Germany_-_Houston_Museum_of_Natural_Science_-_DSC01817.JPG/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Mesurupetala%2C_dragonfly%2C_Late_Late_Jurassic%2C